		<title>Key Takeaways from President Williams’s Interview with the Financial Times</title>
		<link>https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/2023/07/11/key-takeaways-from-president-williamss-interview-with-the-financial-times/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Ellen Simon]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Tue, 11 Jul 2023 14:47:05 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Economic Outlook]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/?p=2531</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[On Tuesday, July 11, The <em>Financial Times</em> published the transcript of an interview with New York Fed President John Williams. In it, he discussed inflation, the labor market, and his economic outlook.]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p class="ts-blog-article-author">
    Ellen Simon</p>



<figure class="lse-featured-image">
	<img decoding="async" loading="eager" width="920" height="576" src="https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/07/ttw-jcw-07112023.jpg?quality=80&amp;w=920" class="cover-image asset-image img-responsive wp-post-image" alt="" post_index="0" srcset="https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/07/ttw-jcw-07112023.jpg 920w, https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/07/ttw-jcw-07112023.jpg?resize=300,188 300w, https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/07/ttw-jcw-07112023.jpg?resize=768,481 768w" sizes="(max-width: 920px) 100vw, 920px" /></figure>



<p>On Tuesday, July 11, The <em>Financial Times</em> published the transcript of an interview with New York Fed President John Williams. In it, he discussed inflation, the labor market, and his economic outlook.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He said:</p>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">“I don’t have a recession in my forecast. I have pretty slow growth.”</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">“[S]ome of the tightening of monetary policy and some effects of credit tightening will weigh on demand in 2024.”</p>
</blockquote>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">In the interview, President Williams said he expects slower economic growth in the second half of the year, as well as the first half of 2024. He indicated that monetary policy is not yet restrictive enough to get inflation to 2 percent, adding that Fed policymakers want to reach that goal in a few years’ time.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He said he expects unemployment to rise to around 4 percent by the end of the year and reach 4.5 percent by the end of next year.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He added that he predicts personal consumption expenditures inflation will come down to around 3 percent this year and reach 2.5 percent in 2024.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://www.ft.com/content/e0d25652-a6ed-46fb-bce7-453219c8e4b4">Read the full transcript (© The Financial Times Limited 2023)</a>.</p>



