		<title>Celebrating Hispanic Heritage at the New York Fed</title>
		<link>https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/2019/10/16/celebrating-hispanic-heritage-at-the-new-york-fed/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Shelley Pitterson, Corporate Communications Senior Analyst, Communications and Outreach]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 16 Oct 2019 12:57:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Diversity & Inclusion]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/?p=1276</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[Communities nationwide celebrate <a href="https://www.hispanicheritagemonth.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Hispanic Heritage Month</a> every fall, highlighting the history, achievements, and contributions of Hispanic and Latinx individuals while recognizing the challenges they face. As President John Williams previously <a href="https://medium.com/new-york-fed/key-takeaways-from-president-williamss-speech-on-diversity-and-inclusion-at-the-open-finance-forum-2dc125d7e657">emphasized</a>, diversity and inclusion is a priority at the New York Fed. This year, the New York Fed celebrated Hispanic Heritage Month through events, work products, and social media campaigns.]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p class="ts-blog-article-author">
    Shelley Pitterson, Corporate Communications Senior Analyst, Communications and Outreach</p>



<figure class="lse-featured-image">
	<img decoding="async" loading="eager" width="1024" height="536" src="https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_hGjb70_QA5K9yeVahRNCwQ.webp?quality=80&amp;w=1024" class="cover-image asset-image img-responsive wp-post-image" alt="" post_index="0" srcset="https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_hGjb70_QA5K9yeVahRNCwQ.webp 1100w, https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_hGjb70_QA5K9yeVahRNCwQ.webp?resize=300,157 300w, https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_hGjb70_QA5K9yeVahRNCwQ.webp?resize=768,402 768w, https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_hGjb70_QA5K9yeVahRNCwQ.webp?resize=1024,536 1024w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>



<p>Communities nationwide celebrate <a href="https://www.hispanicheritagemonth.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Hispanic Heritage Month</a> every fall, highlighting the history, achievements, and contributions of Hispanic and Latinx individuals while recognizing the challenges they face. As President John Williams previously <a href="https://medium.com/new-york-fed/key-takeaways-from-president-williamss-speech-on-diversity-and-inclusion-at-the-open-finance-forum-2dc125d7e657">emphasized</a>, diversity and inclusion is a priority at the New York Fed. This year, the New York Fed celebrated Hispanic Heritage Month through events, work products, and social media campaigns.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="9613"><strong>Resource Networks</strong></h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph" id="5fd1">Over the course of Hispanic Heritage Month, the New York Fed’s&nbsp;<a href="https://www.newyorkfed.org/aboutthefed/diversity.html" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">Office of Diversity and Inclusion</a>, in partnership with two employee resource networks — AALMA (African-American and Latino Men’s Alliance) and MOSAIC (Mentoring Opportunities, Support, Advancement, Inspiration and Chance for African-American and Latina Women) — hosted a series of events highlighting and celebrating the experiences of Latinx people.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph" id="e5c0">This series, titled “A Seat at La Mesa” featured discussions with leading Hispanic researchers, educators, and executives, who spoke about their career paths and the life experiences that shaped who they are today. Participants shared how their heritage and culture influenced their perspectives, and spoke on their experiences being Latinx in today’s world.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="1870"><strong>Educational Comic Book</strong></h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph" id="1e5c">As part of continuing efforts to increase financial literacy, the New York Fed released&nbsp;<a href="https://www.newyorkfed.org/outreach-and-education/comic-books-spanish.html" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank"><em>Había una Vez un Banco</em></a>, the Spanish translation of&nbsp;<a href="https://www.newyorkfed.org/medialibrary/media/outreach-and-education/comic-books/NewYorkFed-OnceUponADime-WebFullColor.pdf" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank"><em>Once Upon A Dime</em></a>, one of the New York Fed’s&nbsp;<a href="https://www.newyorkfed.org/outreach-and-education/comic-books" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">educational comic books</a>. The comic book tells the story of a growing economy on Planet Novus and focuses on concepts of barter, currency, and banking.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="477" height="254" src="https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_8okBUCF-B9KoasIQtIcW4A.webp" alt="" class="wp-image-1289" srcset="https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_8okBUCF-B9KoasIQtIcW4A.webp 477w, https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_8okBUCF-B9KoasIQtIcW4A.webp?resize=300,160 300w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 477px) 100vw, 477px" /></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph" id="0bac"><em>Había una Vez un Banco</em>&nbsp;and the accompanying&nbsp;<a href="https://www.newyorkfed.org/medialibrary/media/outreach-and-education/comic-books/NewYorkFed_HUVUB_Secundaria_HighSchool.pdf" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">lesson plans</a>&nbsp;are intended for Spanish-speaking classrooms and communities across the Second District, serving as a&nbsp;<a href="https://medium.com/new-york-fed/comic-books-as-a-teaching-tool-making-the-language-of-economics-universal-a5bf02ef04f8">resource for educators</a>&nbsp;to teach students about basic economic principles and the role of the Federal Reserve.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="3bed"><strong>Investment Connection</strong></h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph" id="f52d">The New York Fed also kicked off the first phase of its&nbsp;<a href="https://www.newyorkfed.org/outreach-and-education/community-development/community-development-finance/investment-connection-puerto-rico" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">Investment Connection</a>&nbsp;program in Puerto Rico. This Community Development Finance (CoDeFi) program is designed to boost investments in community development financing by connecting local stakeholders to banks and other capital providers.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="607" height="402" src="https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_42DN9hb0ykaLlmd_r4AJ3g.webp" alt="" class="wp-image-1290" srcset="https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_42DN9hb0ykaLlmd_r4AJ3g.webp 607w, https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_42DN9hb0ykaLlmd_r4AJ3g.webp?resize=300,199 300w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 607px) 100vw, 607px" /></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph" id="0ef3">In this first stage of the program, the CoDeFi team will assist and advise local nonprofit organizations on their economic development proposals. This phase is the first step toward the program’s long-term goal of increasing the funding to these organizations and subsequently their capacity, by connecting them to mainland financial institutions.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph" id="befd">Medium posts about the Investment Connection program are available in&nbsp;<a href="https://medium.com/new-york-fed/c%C3%B3mo-incentivar-las-inversiones-en-desarrollo-comunitario-en-puerto-rico-a1264a27e01b">Spanish</a>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<a href="https://medium.com/new-york-fed/enhancing-community-development-investments-in-puerto-rico-2494948e0336">English</a>.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="d27e"><strong>#HispanicHeritageMonth Social Profiles</strong></h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph" id="867a">To mark Hispanic Heritage Month, the New York Fed <a href="https://twitter.com/NewYorkFed/status/1173628305314127878?s=20" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">highlighted</a> several employees on Twitter and LinkedIn. In these profiles, employees shared their stories, reflected on their accomplishments, and expressed what their Hispanic heritage means to them.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph" id="1f50">A few examples:</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" height="543" width="1024" src="https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_fi8Mh7zik2SZGbsxVoX1BQ.webp?w=1024" alt="" class="wp-image-1291" srcset="https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_fi8Mh7zik2SZGbsxVoX1BQ.webp 1100w, https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_fi8Mh7zik2SZGbsxVoX1BQ.webp?resize=300,159 300w, https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_fi8Mh7zik2SZGbsxVoX1BQ.webp?resize=768,407 768w, https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_fi8Mh7zik2SZGbsxVoX1BQ.webp?resize=1024,543 1024w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" height="540" width="1024" src="https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1__vwfOM8IAL9W6woEeeX5wg.webp?w=1024" alt="" class="wp-image-1292" srcset="https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1__vwfOM8IAL9W6woEeeX5wg.webp 1100w, https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1__vwfOM8IAL9W6woEeeX5wg.webp?resize=300,158 300w, https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1__vwfOM8IAL9W6woEeeX5wg.webp?resize=768,405 768w, https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1__vwfOM8IAL9W6woEeeX5wg.webp?resize=1024,540 1024w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" height="540" width="1024" src="https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_wIiKPn9jUcdvtSUcykf-BQ.webp?w=1024" alt="" class="wp-image-1293" srcset="https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_wIiKPn9jUcdvtSUcykf-BQ.webp 1100w, https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_wIiKPn9jUcdvtSUcykf-BQ.webp?resize=300,158 300w, https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_wIiKPn9jUcdvtSUcykf-BQ.webp?resize=768,405 768w, https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_wIiKPn9jUcdvtSUcykf-BQ.webp?resize=1024,540 1024w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" height="542" width="1024" src="https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_LClVrwVoY_ujtz60sWIWJA.webp?w=1024" alt="" class="wp-image-1294" srcset="https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_LClVrwVoY_ujtz60sWIWJA.webp 1100w, https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_LClVrwVoY_ujtz60sWIWJA.webp?resize=300,159 300w, https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_LClVrwVoY_ujtz60sWIWJA.webp?resize=768,406 768w, https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_LClVrwVoY_ujtz60sWIWJA.webp?resize=1024,542 1024w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>



