		<item>
		<title>Meet Our Summer Interns — and Apply Soon for Next Year’s Programs</title>
		<link>https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/2019/09/06/meet-our-summer-interns-and-apply-soon-for-next-years-programs/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Shelley Pitterson, Corporate Communications Senior Analyst]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Fri, 06 Sep 2019 16:38:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[general]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/?p=1309</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[This summer, students from across the country and around the world joined the New York Fed as a part of our Undergraduate Summer Analyst and Graduate Summer Associate Programs. <a href="https://www.newyorkfed.org/careers/summer-programs.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">These programs</a> provide outstanding students with the opportunity to gain valuable work experience in public service by spending a summer working for the New York Fed.]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p class="ts-blog-article-author">
    Shelley Pitterson, Corporate Communications Senior Analyst</p>



<figure class="lse-featured-image">
	<img decoding="async" loading="eager" width="640" height="426" src="https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_t09vM0egNsq2TqXYySa8hQ.webp?quality=80&amp;w=640" class="cover-image asset-image img-responsive wp-post-image" alt="" post_index="0" srcset="https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_t09vM0egNsq2TqXYySa8hQ.webp 640w, https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_t09vM0egNsq2TqXYySa8hQ.webp?resize=300,200 300w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" /></figure>



<p>This summer, students from across the country and around the world joined the New York Fed as a part of our Undergraduate Summer Analyst and Graduate Summer Associate Programs. <a href="https://www.newyorkfed.org/careers/summer-programs.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">These programs</a> provide outstanding students with the opportunity to gain valuable work experience in public service by spending a summer working for the New York Fed.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph" id="baa5">As the end of summer draws near, we’re already looking ahead to next year.&nbsp;<strong>Applications are due September 15 for our new Sophomore Career Exploration Program.&nbsp;</strong>For all other programs, applications are due November 1. Learn more about all the professional opportunities available to students and apply&nbsp;<a href="https://www.newyorkfed.org/careers/summer-programs.html" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">here</a>.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph" id="a912">So, what is the experience of New York Fed summer interns?</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<iframe loading="lazy" title="What It Means to be an Intern at the New York Fed" width="500" height="281" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/RO4KWhOyLYk?feature=oembed" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe>
</div></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph" id="8d26">During their time here, summer analysts and associates are able to enhance their business skills through financial analyses, formal presentations, and research. Each intern is placed with a team within one of the New York Fed’s many groups, such as Statistics, Markets, Research, or Supervision, among others. In these positions, they are responsible for supporting their teams’ day-to-day business and for long-term projects. More than 40% of the summer intern class came from within the Federal Reserve’s Second District.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph" id="bdf0">These programs can also serve as a launchpad for careers, including full-time roles at the New York Fed. In fact, our summer programs are the largest pipeline for entry-level hiring, with many of our interns receiving full-time offers. Of those that do, over 80% accept — a share that speaks to how much they value their work experience here.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph" id="3f5f">Next year, we’re expanding our summer offerings with the new <a href="https://www.newyorkfed.org/careers/student-programs-and-internships">Sophomore Career Exploration Program</a>. To date, our undergraduate summer programs have been primarily focused on rising seniors. But now, as a part of the Sophomore Career Exploration Program, students completing their sophomore year will have the opportunity to work with us and explore career opportunities across one of three tracks: Policy, Business, or Technology.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph" id="099e">Set to launch in 2020, the Sophomore Career Exploration Program aims to help students develop personal and professional skills that will support their success in the workforce. These interns will be paired with mentors at the New York Fed, and they will learn about the summer analyst program for rising seniors. As noted, applications for the new Sophomore Career Exploration Program are due September 15.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph" id="37cc">This year, several interns took over the&nbsp;<a href="https://twitter.com/i/moments/1153771028105109511" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">New York Fed’s Twitter account</a>, sharing tweets and selfies that chronicled their experiences. A growing number of interns have participated in the takeover campaign since it first launched four years ago, and a few of our 2019 interns are featured below.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph" id="c9bb">These summer programs are not the New York Fed’s only initiatives focused on economic education and workforce development, issues that are top priorities for the New York Fed and the Federal Reserve System. Other examples of our work in these areas include the&nbsp;<a href="https://medium.com/new-york-fed/investing-in-americas-workforce-update-on-regional-and-national-efforts-5a33fa1bb6e">Investing in America’s Workforce Initiative</a>, research on&nbsp;<a href="https://www.newyorkfed.org/outreach-and-education/community-development/workforce-development/employer-engagement-community-colleges-report-2018" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">employer engagement by community colleges in New York State</a>, and the&nbsp;<a href="https://www.newyorkfed.org/education/fedchallenge_college.html" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">College Fed Challenge</a>.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="1ea0"><strong>Select Profiles from the 2019 Twitter Takeover</strong></h3>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="9769"><strong>Graduate Summer Associate Program</strong></h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph" id="b4ca"><em><strong>Alicia</strong><br></em>• Home states: Florida &amp; Indiana<br>• Group: Data and Statistics<br>• Studies: Pursuing an MBA with a concentration in Finance</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="560" height="400" src="https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_N7Haf90rSoLntq3o93R-jQ.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-1391" srcset="https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_N7Haf90rSoLntq3o93R-jQ.jpg 560w, https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_N7Haf90rSoLntq3o93R-jQ.jpg?resize=300,214 300w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 560px) 100vw, 560px" /></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph" id="bc23"><strong><em>Mario<br></em></strong>• Home states: Michigan &amp; Texas<br>• Group: Markets<br>• Studies: Pursuing an MBA</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="560" height="426" src="https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_9BiDP6xLMz1ClSv7JhMKdg.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-1390" srcset="https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_9BiDP6xLMz1ClSv7JhMKdg.jpg 560w, https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_9BiDP6xLMz1ClSv7JhMKdg.jpg?resize=300,228 300w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 560px) 100vw, 560px" /></figure>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="ba64"><strong>Undergraduate Summer Analyst Program</strong></h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph" id="748e"><strong><em>Kyra<br></em></strong>• Home state: California<br>• Group: Research<br>• Studies: BA in Economics and History</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="560" height="377" src="https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_5m9U_lyRu7Moq20wlICAXA.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-1388" srcset="https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_5m9U_lyRu7Moq20wlICAXA.jpg 560w, https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_5m9U_lyRu7Moq20wlICAXA.jpg?resize=300,202 300w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 560px) 100vw, 560px" /></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph" id="c61c"><strong><em>Youssouf<br></em></strong>• Home country: Guinea<br>• Group: Technology<br>• Studies: BA in Information System Management</p>



