					<description><![CDATA[On June 18, the New York Fed will host its <a href="https://www.newyorkfed.org/governance-and-culture-reform/culture-and-behavior-in-the-financial-services-industry" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">fourth conference</a> focused on reforming culture and behavior in the financial services industry. <a href="https://www.newyorkfed.org/medialibrary/media/governance-and-culture-reform/culture-conference-agenda-may-2018" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Speakers and panelists</a> will look at progress to date and the challenges ahead, building on the conversation that started with our first event in 2014.]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p class="ts-blog-article-author">
    Brian Manning, Media Relations Associate, Communications and Outreach</p>



<figure class="lse-featured-image">
	<img decoding="async" loading="eager" width="828" height="552" src="https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_GHcB0eBwfjFpmitcfkyK5g.webp?quality=80&amp;w=828" class="cover-image asset-image img-responsive wp-post-image" alt="" post_index="0" srcset="https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_GHcB0eBwfjFpmitcfkyK5g.webp 828w, https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_GHcB0eBwfjFpmitcfkyK5g.webp?resize=300,200 300w, https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2023/06/1_GHcB0eBwfjFpmitcfkyK5g.webp?resize=768,512 768w" sizes="(max-width: 828px) 100vw, 828px" /></figure>



<p>On June 18, the New York Fed will host its <a href="https://www.newyorkfed.org/governance-and-culture-reform/culture-and-behavior-in-the-financial-services-industry" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">fourth conference</a> focused on reforming culture and behavior in the financial services industry. <a href="https://www.newyorkfed.org/medialibrary/media/governance-and-culture-reform/culture-conference-agenda-may-2018" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Speakers and panelists</a> will look at progress to date and the challenges ahead, building on the conversation that started with our first event in 2014.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph" id="45e6">Ahead of the conference, we’ve invited participants to share their views in a series of posts. These essays will explore some of the ideas and questions they hope to discuss.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph" id="a987">The first post will come later today from Kevin Stiroh, head of Supervision at the New York Fed. He will examine the unique role of supervisors in reforming culture.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph" id="b261"><a href="https://tellerwindow.newyorkfed.org/banking-culture/">Check back here</a> over the next two weeks for more essays in this series.</p>



